## 1. [Tags & Macros](#1-tags--macros)  

#### 1.1. [Tags](#1-1-tags)  

- Purpose: Tags are an essential Gravwell concept. Every entry has a single tag associated with it; these tags allow us to separate and categorize data at a basic level.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/ingesters/ingesters.html#tags>)  
- The MongoDB Diagnostics Kit for Gravwell makes use of the following tags:  
- Total: ***1***  
    - mongodb-diag: Tag used for all MongoDB Diagnostics data; necessary for any queries within the Gravwell MongoDB Diagnostics Kit to run properly for dashboards, query library, and templates.  
        - Usage: `tag=mongodb-diag`  

#### 1.2. [Autoextractors](#1-2-autoextractors)  

- Purpose: Autoextractors are simply definitions that can be applied to tags and describe how to correctly extract fields from the data in a given tag. The *ax* module then automatically invokes the appropriate functionality of other modules.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/configuration/autoextractors.html>)  
- The MongoDB Diagnostics Kit for Gravwell makes use of the following autoextractors:  
- Total: ***1***  
    - mongodb-diag: Gravwell-generated JSON extraction for tag mongodb-diag  

#### 1.3. [Macros](#1-3-macros)  

- Purpose: Search macros are a powerful feature that can help you use Gravwell more effectively. Macros can turn long, repetitive search queries into easily-remembered shortcuts.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/search/macros.html>)  
- The MongoDB Diagnostics Kit for Gravwell makes use of the following macros:  
- Total: ***10***  
    - GRAVWELL\_INSTANCE: Configuration Macro; Necessary for alerts within the MongoDB Kit to run properly; >:<change_to_your_specific_port>/  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG: Configuration Macro; Tag used for MongoDB Diagnostics structured log data.  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_ALERT\_META: Alert metadata macro for MongoDB Diagnostics alert titles and context tables.  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_ALERT\_RECIPIENT: This is the address to which MongoDB Alert Flows will be sent to.  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_ALERT\_SENDER: This is the address to which MongoDB Alert Flows will be sent from.  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_COMPONENT\_LOOKUP: Lookup macro used to enrich MongoDB Diagnostics events with structured log component metadata.  
        - Usage: 
        ```
        tag=$MONGODB_DIAG ax
        $MONGODB_DIAG_COMPONENT_LOOKUP 
        | table component componentDescription componentParent
        ```
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_ENRICH\_COMMON: Common enrichment macro for MongoDB Diagnostics alerts and investigation templates.  
    - $MONGODB_DIAG_NORMALIZE_SERVICE: This macro normalizes Service from an abbreviation to the full word.  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_RISK\_SCORE: Risk scoring macro for MongoDB Diagnostics events based on severity, component, diagnostic message, and slow operation context.  
    - MONGODB\_DIAG\_SEVERITY\_LOOKUP: Lookup macro used to enrich MongoDB Diagnostics events with structured log severity names.  
     - Usage: 
        ```
        tag=$MONGODB_DIAG ax
        $MONGODB_DIAG_SEVERITY_LOOKUP 
        | table severity severityName severityDescription
        ```

